@startuml
!include style.iuml
title Per-operation worker lifecycle
hide empty description
[*] --> Queued : immutable\nrevision request
Queued --> Running : worker ready;\nslot available
Queued --> Cancelled : cancel / superseded\nbefore dispatch
Running --> Completed : native result
Running --> Failed : typed error / invalid output
Running --> Cancelled : cooperative cancellation
Running --> Terminating : timeout / crash /\nblocking cancel
Terminating --> Cancelled : cancel;\nreject pending
Terminating --> Failed : timeout / crash;\nreject pending
Completed --> Published : revision + artifact/\nprofile still match
Completed --> Discarded : stale /\ncancelled request
Published --> [*]
Discarded --> [*]
Failed --> [*]
Cancelled --> [*]
note right of Terminating
Terminate; reject pending map.
Next dispatch uses fresh worker.
Do not abandon active native calls.
end note
note bottom of Completed
Progress is not terminal.
Ignore late terminated-job replies.
Worker and job lifetimes differ.
end note
@enduml
